# WHITELIST REPO — everything is untracked unless re-included below
#
# THIS FILE SERVES TWO TREES, and reading it as one list is how it gets broken (#136). It governs
# THIS repository, where every file now lives under estate/, under dev/, or in the root-pinned set;
# and it SHIPS as an estate's own whitelist, where the laid-down tree has no estate/ prefix at all.
# So the re-includes come in two blocks, and each block is dead in the other tree BY DESIGN:
#   * the REPOSITORY block re-includes the two trees and the root-pinned files. In an installed
#     estate estate/ and dev/ do not exist, so those two lines match nothing there.
#   * the ESTATE block re-includes the estate's own top-level record set. In THIS repository those
#     paths sit under estate/, so these lines match nothing here — they are not stale, they are the
#     shipped contract, and deleting them would leave every installed estate ignoring its records.
# A re-include whose subject has left BOTH roots is deleted rather than left as a false claim; the
# development surfaces that moved into dev/ (the method doc, the decision records, the loop
# templates, the history folder, the roster review) were exactly that, and their lines are gone.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.github/

# --- REPOSITORY block — the two trees this repository is split into (#136) ----------------------
!/estate/
!/dev/

# --- ESTATE block — the record set an installed estate re-includes at ITS root -------------------
!/SPEC.md
!/setup.md
!/folder-structure.md
!/folder-map.md
!/installing.md
!/install.sh
!/VERSION
!/_agents/
!/_harness/
!/Tickets/
!/General AI-Knowledge/
!/General Human Knowledge/

# working bulk inside tickets is never a record. TWO SPELLINGS, because a pattern carrying a
# separator is anchored to this file's own directory: the bare form is the estate's, the
# estate/-prefixed form is this repository's, and neither reaches the other's tree.
Tickets/*/Logs/*
Tickets/*/Dump/*
!Tickets/*/Logs/.gitkeep
!Tickets/*/Dump/.gitkeep
estate/Tickets/*/Logs/*
estate/Tickets/*/Dump/*
!estate/Tickets/*/Logs/.gitkeep
!estate/Tickets/*/Dump/.gitkeep

# OS noise + objective editor/tool junk — never records, safe to ignore everywhere (no data
# extensions: the user's own files stay tracked/sovereign). .DS_Store already covered above.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.tmp
*~
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db
